WEBVTT

00:01.430 --> 00:07.120
Long ago, the cave here was home to 
the prosperous Cavern Nation of Romonon,

00:07.120 --> 00:10.350
which specialized in 
delicate magic craftsmanship.

00:11.460 --> 00:14.690
The Romonons clad themselves 
in magical gold works of art

00:14.690 --> 00:17.100
and wore their arrogance 
on their sleeves.

00:17.100 --> 00:20.520
They thought of themselves as a better 
breed than the nations outside,

00:20.520 --> 00:23.770
and looked down on those 
who visited them.

00:24.630 --> 00:27.470
As rumor spread of the 
Romonons' prosperity,

00:27.470 --> 00:30.110
more travelers from 
the surface came to visit.

00:30.110 --> 00:33.760
So, to welcome those they deemed 
a benefit to their society,

00:33.760 --> 00:35.980
they created the Serpentback Road,

00:35.980 --> 00:38.070
a path that only the worthy could travel.

00:38.660 --> 00:42.090
And so that the unworthy 
who could not traverse the road

00:42.090 --> 00:44.670
could never reach Romonon,

00:44.670 --> 00:48.070
they engraved the cave with a maze spell.

00:48.720 --> 00:51.640
The city of Romonon grew ever 
more beautiful and prosperous,

00:51.640 --> 00:54.070
and its people ever more 
haughty and exclusive,

00:54.070 --> 00:55.720
until one day...

00:55.720 --> 00:59.800
when the Romonons began to turn 
their judgment on each other.

01:00.840 --> 01:05.790
Those deemed to be without merit were 
forced to exchange their flesh and blood,

01:06.310 --> 01:10.030
and, through magic, be turned into 
gold statues to decorate their city.

01:10.770 --> 01:13.530
Soon after, just as stagnant 
water becomes foul,

01:13.530 --> 01:16.310
the closed-off Romonon society 
became plagued by malaise.

01:17.000 --> 01:21.360
Internal feuding made 
its people tired and weak.

01:21.690 --> 01:25.600
In the end, it is said, it collapsed 
under the weight of its own gold.

01:26.470 --> 01:32.580
Now all that remains is the labyrinthine 
cave and the Serpentback Road within.

01:34.320 --> 01:36.580
Humans are terrifying creatures.

01:36.930 --> 01:42.610
Equally terrifying is how few of us 
realize what we're capable of.

01:44.050 --> 01:45.540
But Master...

01:47.090 --> 01:50.210
You said magic exists to 
make people happy, right?

01:50.870 --> 01:54.970
It's a power used to help people 
and bring color to the world, right?!

01:57.330 --> 02:01.850
If you witches of the future 
believe that, then...

02:02.720 --> 02:05.350
Yes, I'm sure it will be.

02:07.450 --> 02:08.590
But...

02:08.960 --> 02:13.200
This magic might create an 
unhappy result for our meal today.

02:13.950 --> 02:17.440
Oh, no! It's burning!

02:18.140 --> 02:19.350
Ow, hot!

02:19.350 --> 02:21.570
It's edible once you 
scrape off the burned parts!

02:21.570 --> 02:22.500
So good!

02:22.860 --> 02:26.020
<i>Magic is a power to bring 
color to the world...</i>

02:23.100 --> 02:24.300
So good!

02:24.550 --> 02:26.840
Hey, Brushbuddy, have some!

02:27.270 --> 02:30.000
<i>I hope that's true.</i>

02:27.650 --> 02:28.800
What a big bone!

02:31.090 --> 02:32.560
<i>I truly do.</i>

04:06.710 --> 04:09.390
Well, how will you proceed?

04:09.890 --> 04:14.060
As test proctor, I can't give 
any more advice past this point.

04:10.190 --> 04:15.400
<b>The Shadow of Romonon</b>

04:14.060 --> 04:17.790
It's twisty, but it's 
still a single road ahead.

04:17.790 --> 04:19.410
It's easy.

04:20.630 --> 04:22.550
Just fly through and—

04:30.050 --> 04:31.210
Look out!

04:36.130 --> 04:38.170
They're standing sideways?

04:38.170 --> 04:40.050
Is that your spell?

04:40.560 --> 04:42.930
No, it's the magic of the road.

04:43.340 --> 04:46.200
Orientation is all 
topsy-turvy in this cave.

04:46.200 --> 04:50.940
You can only stand straight 
when you're on the serpent's back.

04:50.940 --> 04:54.940
If you step off the road, you'll fall 
into the labyrinth of the grander cave,

04:54.940 --> 04:57.490
and eventually end up 
back at the entrance.

04:58.450 --> 04:59.820
Hang on...

05:00.240 --> 05:02.570
These serpent-scale paving stones...

05:03.490 --> 05:05.950
Are they all casting seals?

05:07.200 --> 05:10.710
But they're cracked and worn in places...

05:11.380 --> 05:15.980
I didn't realize that my first 
time through and fell off.

05:16.360 --> 05:19.840
Th-The right answer here is a spell 
from the Basics of Casting Primer...

05:19.840 --> 05:21.380
I know the one.

05:30.290 --> 05:32.920
Water flows, directed by gravity.

05:32.920 --> 05:35.670
It stops when it reaches level ground.

05:36.700 --> 05:40.400
If the only places that are level 
are places where the seals are intact,

05:40.790 --> 05:45.340
the pooled water will indicate 
where it's safe to step.

05:46.140 --> 05:48.160
You got it totally right!

05:48.160 --> 05:50.820
You really live up to the Arklaum name.

05:51.160 --> 05:54.770
E-Even on my second time 
through, I didn't realize...

05:54.770 --> 05:56.420
<i>The "right" answer...</i>

05:56.940 --> 05:58.640
<i>The "right" spell...</i>

05:59.900 --> 06:01.650
<i>The "right" path...</i>

06:02.490 --> 06:08.700
<i>Always sticking to what's "right" 
is what I don't want to do.</i>

06:08.700 --> 06:10.770
Hey now, Richehlette.

06:11.610 --> 06:14.540
Look at you, drawing more 
of these worthless spells.

06:14.900 --> 06:18.400
You'll never become 
a proper witch like this.

06:18.980 --> 06:22.530
Why can't you just do 
what your master tells you?

06:23.890 --> 06:26.030
These ridiculous scribbles...

06:26.030 --> 06:27.300
Throw them out!

06:30.730 --> 06:32.210
<i>I don't want to.</i>

06:32.790 --> 06:34.810
<i>They're not scribbles.</i>

06:34.810 --> 06:37.160
<i>These are my spells!</i>

06:38.630 --> 06:41.010
<i>I don't want to throw out who I am.</i>

06:41.010 --> 06:42.740
<i>Which means...</i>

06:44.930 --> 06:47.220
This way. Come along.

06:49.520 --> 06:54.100
I know the way through, 
but the myrphon won't follow.

06:54.450 --> 06:57.410
Come on. I don't want you falling off.

06:57.410 --> 06:59.400
Just follow me already.

07:05.270 --> 07:08.650
Don't try to win me over with 
your cute little mannerisms!

07:08.650 --> 07:09.980
B-But...

07:10.990 --> 07:13.000
The mannerisms are important.

07:13.470 --> 07:16.500
Myrphons vocalize to
 communicate with each other.

07:16.500 --> 07:19.790
So the right answer to get them to follow

07:19.790 --> 07:23.680
is to use an echoing spell 
that mimics their cries...

07:27.600 --> 07:30.230
There's no "right answer" with magic.

07:31.390 --> 07:34.390
There's no rule saying 
it has to be some way.

07:34.390 --> 07:36.140
The myrphons...

07:36.140 --> 07:39.780
You may have taken this test before,

07:39.780 --> 07:42.650
but I wish you'd stop blathering 
on about "right answers"

07:42.650 --> 07:45.920
and telling us what to do 
before we even try.

07:46.660 --> 07:48.890
I want to be myself.

07:48.890 --> 07:51.930
I don't want to become
a witch who isn't me.

07:52.830 --> 07:58.170
So I'll reach the end of this 
road using only my own spells.

07:58.170 --> 07:59.640
Richeh...

08:01.190 --> 08:03.920
But... you can't.

08:04.650 --> 08:07.330
That's just not how the world works.

08:07.330 --> 08:11.930
And this is a test, 
so it has "right answers."

08:12.550 --> 08:16.240
We're apprentices, 
and inexperienced, and children,

08:16.240 --> 08:18.860
so we have to do it by the book...

08:18.860 --> 08:21.170
If I don't, I'll fail again.

08:21.170 --> 08:23.780
That's just how a test—

08:23.780 --> 08:26.750
That's exactly the kind 
of talk that I hate!

08:26.750 --> 08:30.290
But if you use a spell that hasn't 
been tested, it could fail...

08:30.290 --> 08:32.130
If I do it so it'll work, it'll work!

08:32.130 --> 08:33.330
That's too reckless!

08:33.330 --> 08:36.580
Learn from your failures, 
and it becomes knowledge.

08:36.580 --> 08:38.580
Knowledge that fuels future success.

08:39.410 --> 08:42.440
I happen to know someone 
who learns that way.

08:43.640 --> 08:45.950
Do things your way, Richeh.

08:46.590 --> 08:48.220
It doesn't matter to me.

08:48.760 --> 08:51.270
I don't need your permission 
to do that, Agott.

09:08.360 --> 09:11.150
What's that sound? The water?

09:15.120 --> 09:19.460
M-My master tells me every day...

09:20.100 --> 09:21.620
"You can't do it."

09:21.620 --> 09:23.330
"It's beyond you."

09:24.130 --> 09:25.540
I agree with him.

09:26.530 --> 09:30.270
So... I've studied how other 
people do things instead.

09:31.470 --> 09:33.540
But I guess I really can't do it.

09:34.920 --> 09:37.090
Because this is Romonon...

09:39.630 --> 09:44.930
It's a road created to prevent 
the unworthy from entering.

09:50.850 --> 09:52.860
Coco? What's wrong?

09:53.240 --> 09:57.990
Master Qifrey, are there 
other witches here today?

09:57.990 --> 10:01.880
Kukrow left, so I don't think so.

10:01.880 --> 10:03.130
Why do you ask?

10:03.130 --> 10:06.920
I thought I saw a robed 
figure over there just now.

10:07.910 --> 10:08.830
Coco?

10:21.060 --> 10:23.460
<i>But of course there's no one here, right?</i>

10:23.460 --> 10:24.810
Coco!

10:25.570 --> 10:28.570
Right! On my way!

10:39.970 --> 10:44.780
The water drops off and 
winds in the strangest ways...

10:45.330 --> 10:47.220
The casting seals that 
maintain orientation

10:47.220 --> 10:51.210
have no effect over the gap in the road.

10:51.680 --> 10:54.100
We have to find our own way across.

10:55.220 --> 10:56.230
Richeh?

10:56.230 --> 11:00.180
The casting seals only work when 
we're standing on the stones.

11:00.180 --> 11:03.850
So we just have to extend 
the stones to the other side.

11:06.880 --> 11:08.230
Like this.

11:18.260 --> 11:21.080
Sh-She's riding a ribbon made of stone?!

11:24.520 --> 11:25.840
There.

11:25.840 --> 11:30.090
If there's something you can't do, 
change the method to something you can.

11:32.090 --> 11:33.910
She has a point.

11:44.400 --> 11:46.070
Th-That's not safe!

11:46.070 --> 11:47.480
You can't...

11:51.980 --> 11:55.240
A combination of repetition 
and replication spells...

11:55.240 --> 11:58.310
It makes for a narrow path, 
but it really worked!

12:00.870 --> 12:02.190
Agott!

12:02.190 --> 12:03.120
I'm okay!

12:08.370 --> 12:14.480
<i>It's hard to draw clean lines under my 
cloak, so the spell faded quickly.</i>

12:14.480 --> 12:16.210
<i>I still have a long way to go.</i>

12:16.210 --> 12:18.160
<i>I have to work even harder!</i>

12:18.760 --> 12:20.810
You did well.

12:20.810 --> 12:22.760
It was easy.

12:23.790 --> 12:25.520
Looks like it's your turn.

12:30.720 --> 12:33.310
I...

12:34.270 --> 12:36.150
I just can't do it!

12:37.650 --> 12:39.460
I'm not cut out for this!

12:39.460 --> 12:43.910
I don't have any talent, courage, 
confidence, aptitude, skill... nothing!

12:44.260 --> 12:46.960
And with the road broken, 
I don't even have luck!

12:46.960 --> 12:49.790
I'm going to fail again!

12:48.600 --> 12:49.790
Oh, come on.

12:49.790 --> 12:54.550
You've already demonstrated 
incredible analysis and knowledge!

12:54.550 --> 12:58.050
If you've done this twice before, 
put that experience to good use!

12:58.460 --> 13:00.680
Just draw a spell already! Anything!

13:13.860 --> 13:15.800
The myrphon cry spell?

13:17.360 --> 13:19.810
A rain spell to make puddles...

13:21.020 --> 13:24.700
Why are you using spells for 
problems we've solved already?!

13:24.700 --> 13:27.280
You need something new to cross over!

13:28.310 --> 13:30.710
I-I can't draw.

13:30.710 --> 13:32.210
What?

13:32.210 --> 13:34.460
M-My...

13:34.790 --> 13:37.470
M-My hands won't stop shaking.

13:39.460 --> 13:45.470
I-I've never been able to draw 
right when someone else is watching.

13:45.860 --> 13:49.720
The thought of their eyes on me 
makes me start to sweat and tremble...

13:49.720 --> 13:54.860
Then I mess up the lines, 
and the spells turn out awful.

13:55.290 --> 13:57.860
I want to do something about it...

13:58.340 --> 14:01.230
but I feel so helpless.

14:02.300 --> 14:09.230
A-And the more people see me 
panicking, the worse it becomes.

14:10.990 --> 14:13.350
This time, I thought, 
I'd be able to make it.

14:13.350 --> 14:15.770
I prepared, I studied...

14:15.770 --> 14:20.630
I drew all the "right answer" 
spells in advance.

14:21.110 --> 14:24.980
If I'm alone, I can 
concentrate and draw right.

14:24.980 --> 14:28.180
We're not forbidden from bringing 
our palm quires in with us.

14:29.020 --> 14:32.020
So I only need to close 
the circles to cast the spells.

14:32.020 --> 14:35.100
It would look like I was doing it right.

14:36.520 --> 14:39.620
But I didn't expect a gap in the road.

14:40.370 --> 14:43.530
I've been punished for not doing it right.

14:44.090 --> 14:47.220
Why am I always like this?

14:47.220 --> 14:50.290
You said you want to be yourself...

14:50.290 --> 14:53.650
but I wish I could stop being me.

14:54.010 --> 14:56.920
I wish I could be literally anyone else!

14:59.220 --> 15:02.980
<i>This test is about whether you can 
cast spells in front of Outsiders</i>

15:02.980 --> 15:05.130
<i>without being caught.</i>

15:05.130 --> 15:09.180
<i>Unfortunately, at this rate, 
he'll never be able to pass.</i>

15:09.180 --> 15:10.570
You <i>can</i> do it.

15:11.430 --> 15:14.020
You can do it just as you are.

15:14.510 --> 15:16.490
You said the answer yourself just now.

15:16.870 --> 15:18.190
Didn't you realize?

15:18.740 --> 15:22.940
If you can concentrate and draw when 
you're alone, then be alone right now!

15:24.690 --> 15:26.560
Um...

15:27.130 --> 15:29.260
But how?

15:29.260 --> 15:30.860
However you can!

15:30.860 --> 15:35.090
Magic can make stones 
grow or make rain fall.

15:35.090 --> 15:38.330
You should be able to make 
all kinds of spaces to be alone!

15:38.330 --> 15:41.340
I-I can't draw a spell like that.

15:41.340 --> 15:42.840
Then don't use a spell!

15:44.610 --> 15:47.750
I-I can't figure that out on the spot...

15:47.750 --> 15:50.330
I... I...

16:11.090 --> 16:12.280
Come on!

16:13.410 --> 16:15.410
Don't interfere.

16:17.540 --> 16:21.080
I hate this, I hate this! It's the worst!

16:21.080 --> 16:23.290
I must look so pathetic.

16:23.290 --> 16:26.520
This is the only thing I could 
come up with on the fly...

16:26.520 --> 16:28.990
It's so pathetic, I could cry!

16:28.990 --> 16:31.930
I'm sure they're disgusted by me...

16:32.680 --> 16:34.350
They might be laughing.

16:34.350 --> 16:38.350
I p-probably look ridiculous...

16:38.350 --> 16:42.940
I-I really must look so stupid...

16:43.500 --> 16:46.960
The proctor's probably 
disappointed in me, too.

16:50.030 --> 16:51.570
<i>They're not laughing.</i>

16:52.200 --> 16:56.820
<i>No one's disgusted, or laughing, 
or making fun of me.</i>

16:57.450 --> 16:59.790
<i>No one but me.</i>

17:01.960 --> 17:05.160
<i>Make it something you can do, 
and you can do it.</i>

17:05.800 --> 17:10.640
<i>I get it. The only one casting 
a curse to sabotage me...</i>

17:11.470 --> 17:14.100
<i>was just myself in the mirror.</i>

17:17.700 --> 17:18.950
Mirror...

17:21.760 --> 17:24.860
Right here... No, here?

17:25.750 --> 17:28.360
The casting seal in the 
Mirror Cloak of Borrowshade...

17:29.040 --> 17:30.630
It's not a mirror so much as

17:30.630 --> 17:32.990
an application of signs of 
concealment and reflection.

17:32.990 --> 17:36.280
It conceals the wearer and 
makes them into a "shadow,"

17:36.280 --> 17:40.220
then projects an image of a beast 
reflected in its scales.

17:41.250 --> 17:45.380
That's amazing. 
The spell is so layered...

17:45.380 --> 17:49.760
Oh, but then I... maybe...

18:08.890 --> 18:09.940
What is it?

18:11.150 --> 18:12.340
Euini!

18:13.150 --> 18:14.470
Stay there!

18:14.470 --> 18:15.920
I'll erect a wind barrier!

18:17.780 --> 18:21.180
A Romonon trap? 
Or an ancient, unknown spell?!

18:21.540 --> 18:23.410
I-It's okay!

18:24.110 --> 18:26.920
This is my spell!

18:26.920 --> 18:28.420
Euini?

18:32.850 --> 18:33.830
You...

18:35.130 --> 18:37.070
What happened to your cloak?

18:38.210 --> 18:42.680
When I ducked inside, I could 
see the casting seal inside it...

18:42.680 --> 18:44.960
I erased just the "mirror" part

18:44.960 --> 18:47.740
and made it just a "cloak of borrowshade."

18:48.440 --> 18:52.440
Now I can hide in the dark 
and draw what I need to.

18:52.440 --> 18:56.950
The myrphon can't see me now, so it 
might be harder to bring it along,

18:56.950 --> 18:59.490
but I still have the sound 
spell to mimic its cries.

18:59.490 --> 19:02.320
All that matters is that it 
can't tell I'm human, right?

19:02.320 --> 19:04.190
Well, technically.

19:04.610 --> 19:07.550
Being hidden means being alone.

19:07.550 --> 19:10.590
Now I can concentrate and not 
worry about people looking at me.

19:10.590 --> 19:13.740
I think I can draw like this!

19:28.690 --> 19:32.180
I-It's a little embarrassing 
to do it this way,

19:32.520 --> 19:33.940
but I think...

19:36.120 --> 19:39.070
this might be who I am.

19:44.830 --> 19:47.580
You don't want to not be yourself anymore?

19:48.810 --> 19:51.590
Yeah. A little less, anyway.

19:54.310 --> 19:57.170
Next time, don't just say 
you can't do it right away.

19:57.170 --> 19:59.470
You're not worthless at all.

19:59.470 --> 20:01.580
I-I might still say it...

20:01.580 --> 20:05.080
B-But I'll work hard to keep that 
from being the last word.

20:06.440 --> 20:07.600
U-Um...

20:10.600 --> 20:12.930
Thank you, Richeh.

20:14.840 --> 20:18.110
I thought you didn't have any 
interest in other people.

20:18.110 --> 20:22.920
He saved me first. Now we're even.

20:23.370 --> 20:24.490
Besides...

20:25.500 --> 20:28.250
The feeling of not being 
able to do what you want to...

20:29.580 --> 20:31.110
I understand it, too.

20:33.190 --> 20:36.290
It's natural to be frustrated 
when you can't do something.

20:36.290 --> 20:38.400
That's what lets us improve.

20:39.730 --> 20:42.490
I'm going to become a 
better version of myself.

20:42.490 --> 20:45.850
I could never love an inferior one.

20:49.350 --> 20:52.540
The purpose of tests is 
to learn about yourself.

20:52.540 --> 20:57.360
There's only one path forward, but the 
spells we draw along it are all different.

20:57.360 --> 21:02.420
We all search for our own way, 
and use it to walk the path ahead.

21:03.390 --> 21:05.660
Over and over again.

21:05.660 --> 21:09.250
See? Tests aren't that bad, are they?

21:12.650 --> 21:13.670
But...

21:14.500 --> 21:17.710
Until Master Qifrey apologizes 
for lying and making me take it,

21:17.710 --> 21:20.330
I'm still gonna be mad.

21:20.330 --> 21:22.280
He's earned an Angricheh point.

21:23.240 --> 21:24.840
An Angricheh point?

21:26.010 --> 21:29.160
Oh, right. Speaking of Qifrey...

21:29.820 --> 21:32.410
Lately, has he mentioned—

21:36.320 --> 21:37.820
Master Alaira!

21:36.320 --> 21:37.820
Miss Alaira!

21:37.820 --> 21:39.670
The Brimmed Caps?!

21:42.130 --> 21:43.360
The Brimmed Caps?!

21:48.290 --> 21:49.640
Listen, everyone!

21:49.640 --> 21:51.650
Don't listen to anything 
the Brimmed Caps say!

21:51.650 --> 21:53.200
Don't be led astray!

21:53.200 --> 21:55.170
Run away as fast as you—

21:55.170 --> 21:56.880
Forbidden magic is—

22:01.550 --> 22:03.110
Miss Alaira?

23:35.480 --> 23:40.150
Episode 13:

23:35.480 --> 23:40.150
Forbidden Magic
